From 0b4396a0b3264014f1cc8f2f25c2e35a5fe328a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TuNV <tunguyenvanbn94@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:18:50 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] [icwmp A3] Registry claim conflicts and end of session action
 rollback

R6: two dm modules claiming the same path made dm_registry_owns() answer for
whichever module was scanned first, so the compat bridge filtered on an
arbitrary owner and one of the two trees lost silently.  build() now reports
every overlapping .paths pair once, and dm_registry_conflicts() exposes the
count.  Extending an object another module owns still works the intended way:
declare no .paths and let the merge do it.

R7: setters queue their end of session action (reboot, factory reset,
diagnostic) while the RPC is still being written.  When the RPC then faulted,
the engine reverted UCI and the platform but left the queued actions in the
list, so a rolled back SetParameterValues could still reboot the box.
dm_end_session_mark()/dm_end_session_rollback() drop the actions queued by a
batch that faults, and restore end_session_flag with them.

Also call dm_platform_revert() when the platform batch commit itself fails --
only dmuci_revert() ran there, leaving the platform queue for the next RPC.

NOT build tested: no compiler in this environment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
